      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. I noticed you used \"sublime\" and \"grandeur\" for the landscape, but then pivoted to \"iconography\" and \"identity\" for the masks. While I see the distinction, I'm worried the phrasing for the masks feels a bit more... descriptive and ethnographic rather than being treated as \"High Art\" on the same level as the oil painting. \n\nCould you try rewriting the blurb for Piece B to emphasize its technical complexity and its place in the canon of fine art, rather than just its cultural role? I want to make sure the audience doesn't view it as just a \"cultural artifact\" compared to the painting.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
