      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much better, thanks. It feels more balanced now.\n\nI'm thinking about how to structure the actual gallery flow. For the section featuring the masks, I want to make sure we aren't accidentally implying they are \"primitive\" or \"pre-modern\" just because they lack the oil/canvas tradition. \n\nIn your professional opinion, is there an inherent difference in the \"intellectual depth\" or \"conceptual complexity\" between a Western landscape painting and these types of traditional carvings? I want to know how to defend this exhibit if people argue that the painting is a \"higher\" form of expression than the masks.",
